Regional specialists are also gaining traction. Companies such as TechMAC Co., Ltd. and JoyJet Precision Limited focus on ultra‑small diameters (0.1‑0.3 mm) and have secured contracts with boutique PCB manufacturers in Taiwan and Korea. Chinese firms-including Wuxi Sundi Precision Tools, Guangdong Dtech Technology and Shenzhen Jinzhou Precision Technology-benefit from proximity to emerging fab complexes and government incentives aimed at domesticising high‑value tooling. Their cost‑competitive offerings, supported by aggressive after‑sales service networks, enable them to capture price‑sensitive orders in Southeast Asia and South America.
